<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Native support for A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2).

    That mod places animals in three abstract recipes that only carry a recipeUsers list: ADS_Cat1 (basic
    replacements), ADS_Cat2 (simple prosthetics) and ADS_Cat3 (bionics). The lists are cumulative.
    Its 1.6 Animal_Categories.xml lists the Emu in ADS_Cat1 and ADS_Cat2, and not in ADS_Cat3, next to
    the cassowary, ostrich and turkey. The moa is the emu's variant (same parent, same body plan), so it
    goes where the emu is: categories 1 and 2.

    The guard: the operation runs only when ADS_Cat1 exists, that is when the mod is loaded. A
    PatchOperationConditional with no nomatch succeeds without doing anything otherwise. MayRequire
    cannot be used on an operation: nothing reads it there.

    The load order: ADS 2 copies these lists into its real recipes in its own last patch, so About.xml
    declares loadBefore for it. Order, not a dependency.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>Moa</li>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat2"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>Moa</li>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
